2026-06-30 15:12:38,351 - openai._base_client - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'timeout': 300, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-07fec3b5-643e-493b-b260-d885351ccdcc', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You are an expert SDRF-Proteomics annotator for crosslinking mass spectrometry (XL-MS) datasets.\n\nExtract the following SDRF metadata terms from the provided publication text and/or PRIDE project description.\n\nTERMS TO EXTRACT:\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nterm: disease\nsdrf_column: characteristics[disease]\nontology: EFO:0000408, MONDO, DOID, PATO\ndescription: Disease state of the sample.\ninstructions: For healthy/normal samples use "normal" (PATO:0000461). For diseased\n  samples use MONDO or DOID terms. Return null only if completely unstated.\n  Most XL-MS samples are "normal" unless explicitly studying a disease model.\n\nterm: phenotype\nsdrf_column: characteristics[phenotype]\nontology: EFO:0000651, PATO, EFO\ndescription: Observable characteristics or traits (drug sensitivity, molecular markers,\n  expression phenotypes, environmental responses).\ninstructions: Return null if not stated. This captures how the sample behaves/appears\n  (distinct from disease diagnosis).\n\nterm: treatment\nsdrf_column: characteristics[treatment]\nontology: EFO:0000727, NCIT, EFO\ndescription: Treatment or perturbation applied to the sample (drug, stimulus,\n  environmental stress, growth condition change).\ninstructions: Return null if not stated or not applicable. Examples: "doxycycline\n  treatment", "heat shock", "DMSO vehicle control".\n\nterm: compound\nsdrf_column: characteristics[compound]\nontology: CHEBI:24431, CHEBI, NCIT, EFO\ndescription: Chemical compound or drug applied to the sample.\ninstructions: Use ChEBI if possible. Return null if no compound treatment. Do NOT\n  include the crosslinking reagent here — that goes in comment[cross-linker].\n\nterm: dose\nsdrf_column: characteristics[dose]\nontology: NCIT:C25488\ndescription: Dose or concentration of compound treatment.\npattern: number + unit (e.g. 10 mg/kg, 50 uM, 100 nM, 10 mg/mL)\ninstructions: Return null if no compound treatment or dose not stated.\n\nterm: genetic modification\nsdrf_column: characteristics[genetic modification]\nontology: EFO:0000510, EFO\ndescription: Method of genetic modification (knockout, knockdown, overexpression,\n  transduction). Describes HOW the modification was done.\ninstructions: Return null if not stated.\n\nterm: perturbation\nsdrf_column: characteristics[perturbation]\nontology: PRIDE:0000700\ndescription: Type of perturbation applied (environmental/experimental perturbation).\ninstructions: Return null if not stated or not applicable.\n\nterm: depletion\nsdrf_column: characteristics[depletion]\nontology: PRIDE:0000020\ndescription: Whether abundant protein depletion was performed.\nallowed_values: no depletion, depletion, not applicable\ninstructions: Return "no depletion" if not mentioned. Return "depletion" if\n  high-abundance protein removal is described (e.g. albumin depletion).\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nReturn a single JSON object where each key is the exact sdrf_column string shown above.\nFor each key, return a dict with:\n  "value": the extracted value (string, list, or null)\n  "accession": ontology accession if resolvable, else null\n  "confidence": "high", "medium", or "low"\n  "evidence_quote": short verbatim quote from the text, or null\n  "evidence_location": location in the paper (e.g. "Methods"), or null'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '[TITLE]\nK562 cell lime LC-MSMS,Quantitative measurement of hydrophobicity dependent LLPS property of chromatin condensate\n\n[ABSTRACT]\nK562 cell line treated with 1,6-HD and proteins were captured via cross-linking. We quantified chromatin structure changes and chromatin binding proteins in K562 cell before and after 1,6-hexanediol treatment by Hi-C and Hi-MS, respectively.\n\n[METHODS]\nFor isotonic condition，1,6-Hexanediol was dissolved in RPMI 1640 medium containing 10% FBS to a concentration of 10% to make a storage solution. The working solution was made by dilution using RPMI 1640 medium containing 10% FBS immediately before use. For hypotonic condition, 1,6-Hexanediol was dissolved in H2O to a concentration of 30% to make a storage solution. The working solution was made by 1:2 mix of 30% storage solution and RPMI 1640 medium containing 10% FBS immediately before use. cells were treated at a concentration of 10% for the time indicated. Hi-MS The Hi-MS sample was prepared based on BL-Hi-C protocol to extract chromatin associated proteins. Briefly, 107 K562 cells were incubated with 1% formaldehyde in PBS to crosslink protein–DNA in the cells, then, the cells were suspended using 1% SDS lysis buffer (50 mM HEPES-KOH, 150mM NaCl, 1 mM EDTA, 1% Triton X-100, and 1% SDS). After wash cells with cutsmart buffer with 1%TX-100, the genome was then digested by HaeIII into fragments with blunt-ends. The DNA fragments were treated with adenine and ligated with bridge linker with biotin for 4h at RT. Then, the cells were washed by 0.2%SDS nucleus lysis buffer(20mM Tris-HCl, 50mM NaCl, 2mM EDTA, 0.2% SDS, 1×protease inhibitor) once, then incubate in 0.2%SDS nucleus lysis buffer at 4°C overnight. The next morning, the cells were washed once again and resuspended in 0.2%SDS nucleus lysis buffer. Cells were sonicated using Digital Sonifier Cell Disruptor at 40% output for 24 cycles, each 5s ON and 5s OFF. After sonication, 2x volumes of IP dilution buffer (20mM Tris pH8, 2mM EDTA, 450mM NaCl, 2% Triton X-100, protease inhibitors) was added and incubate for 1hrs at 4C with rotation. The biotinylated linker/DNA/protein complex in supernatant was then incubated with 1ml M280 magnet beads slurry for 2hrs at 4°C with rotation. Beads were then washed 3 times with cold IP wash buffer 1 (20mM Tris pH8, 2mM EDTA, 50mM NaCl, 1% Triton X-100, 0.1% SDS), once with cold TE buffer (1mM Tris pH8, 1mM EDTA). The complex were eluted twice for 5min at 100 °C in 60ul H2O each time and sent for label-free quantitative mass spectrometry (MS) analysis.\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17', 'store': True, 'temperature': 0.3}}
